<title>NEW ZEALAND: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEW ZEALAND GOVERNMENT LIST (970808)</p>
<p>Governor-General (Sworn in 21 Mar 1996)...Michael HARDIE BOYS</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>NATIONAL PARTY-NEW ZEALAND FIRST COALITION GOVERNMENT</p>
<p>(Formed 15 Dec 96. All members of the National Party</p>
<p>	 unless marked NZF)</p>
<p> Prime Minister.....................................Jim BOLGER</p>
<p>(also Minister in charge of the New Zealand</p>
<p>Security Intelligence Service)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister....................Winston PETERS (NZF)</p>
<p>(also Treasurer)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>Agriculture; Forestry; International Trade;</p>
<p>    Contact Energy Ltd..........................Lockwood SMITH</p>
<p>Associate Treasurer; Valuation Department;</p>
<p>    Public Trust Office....................John DELAMERE (NZF)</p>
<p>Attorney General; Audit Department;</p>
<p>    Defence; Corrections; War Pensions...............Paul EAST</p>
<p>Commerce; Fisheries; Lands; Industry;</p>
<p>    Associate Minister of Agriculture..............John LUXTON</p>
<p> Education; Leader of the House...................Wyatt CREECH</p>
<p> Employment...............................Peter McCARDLE (NZF)</p>
<p>Environment; Crown Research Institutes,</p>
<p>Biosecurity; Associate Minister of Foreign</p>
<p>    Affairs and Trade..............................Simon UPTON</p>
<p> Finance; Revenue...................................Bill BIRCH</p>
<p>Foreign Affairs &amp; Trade; Pacific Island</p>
<p>    Affairs; Disarmament and Arms Controls........Don McKINNON</p>
<p> Health...........................................Bill ENGLISH</p>
<p>Housing; Tourism; Sport, Fitness and Leisure...Murray McCULLY</p>
<p>Justice; Courts; Treaty of Waitangi negotiations..Doug GRAHAM</p>
<p>Labour; Immigration; Energy; Business</p>
<p>    Development...................................Max BRADFORD</p>
<p>Maori Affairs; Racing, Associate Minister</p>
<p>    of Sport; Fitness and Leisure.............Tau HENARE (NZF)</p>
<p>Minister in charge of the New Zealand</p>
<p>     Security Intelligence Service..........See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Police; Internal Affairs; Civil Defence......Jack ELDER (NZF)</p>
<p>Research, Science and Technology; Communications;</p>
<p>    Information Technology; Statistics......Maurice WILLIAMSON</p>
<p> Social Welfare....................................Roger SOWRY</p>
<p>State Services; State Owned Enterprises (except</p>
<p>Contact Energy Ltd); Transport; Accident</p>
<p>Rehabilitation and Compensation Insurance;</p>
<p>    responsibility for Radio NZ..................Jenny SHIPLEY</p>
<p> Treasurer...........................See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS OUTSIDE CABINET:</p>
<p>Conservation; Associate Minister of Education;</p>
<p>    Associate Minister of Social Welfare............Nick SMITH</p>
<p>Education Review Office; Associate Minister</p>
<p>    of Education................................Brian DONNELLY</p>
<p> Senior Citizens; Consumer Affairs..............Robyn McDONALD</p>
<p>Women's Affairs; Cultural Affairs; Local</p>
<p>    Government..............................Christine FLETCHER</p>
<p>Youth Affairs; Associate Minister for Accident</p>
<p>Rehabilitation and Compensation Insurance;</p>
<p>    Associate Minister for the Environment......Deborah MORRIS</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Speaker of the House of Representatives.............Doug KIDD</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p> Reserve Bank Governor...............................Don BRASH</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
